<%# Email row.

    Locals: user (required).

    Changing an existing address does NOT write here — it mails a confirmation
    link to the CURRENT address, and the change lands only when the holder of
    that inbox approves it. The button says "Change" and the line underneath says
    where the link goes, because a control that appears to save and then does not
    is worse than one that explains itself.

    Gated on a real delta for the same reason the name row is: an empty field, or
    the address you already have, would spend a real email on nothing. Alpine
    adds the disabled state on init, so a page whose JS never ran still gets a
    working button and the server does the real checks either way.

    An account with no address yet is the exception: nothing to protect, so the
    first one applies directly and the button says Save.
%>
<% has_email = user.email.present? %>
<% current = user.email.to_s.strip %>

<% if has_email %>
  <p class="text-sm text-secondary mb-1">Current address</p>
  <p class="text-heading font-semibold mb-4 break-all"><%= user.email %></p>
<% end %>

<%= form_with url: profile_email_path, method: :patch, scope: :profile,
              data: { turbo: false },
              html: { "x-data": "{ current: #{current.downcase.to_json}, value: '' }" },
              class: "flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3" do |form| %>
  <div class="flex-1 min-w-0" style="min-width: 14rem;">
    <label class="block text-sm text-secondary mb-2 font-medium" for="profile_email">
      <%= has_email ? "New address" : "Email address" %>
    </label>
    <%= form.email_field :email, value: nil, autocomplete: "email",
                         placeholder: "you@example.com", class: "input-field",
                         "x-model": "value" %>
  </div>
  <%= form.submit has_email ? "Change" : "Save",
                  class: "btn btn-primary",
                  ":disabled": "value.trim() === '' || value.trim().toLowerCase() === current",
                  ":class": "(value.trim() === '' || value.trim().toLowerCase() === current) && 'opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed'" %>
<% end %>

<% if has_email %>
  <p class="text-muted text-xs mt-2">
    We'll send a link to <span class="font-semibold"><%= user.email %></span> to approve the change.
    Your address stays the same until you do.
  </p>
<% end %>
